comments.message:
You use this directly below. Before you do so you need to test for error on extraction. Otherwise this risks using an uninitialised value.

```suggestion
	rc = pldm_msgbuf_extract(buf, name->name_string_count);
	if (rc) {
	    return pldm_msgbuf_discard(buf, rc);
	}
```

Both addition operations should have overflow tests. You could also accumulate them serially, which may help:

```suggestion
		names_size += ascii_len;
		names_size += utf16_len;


```

The overflow tests look like:

```
if ((SIZE_MAX - ascii_len) < names_size) { /* error handling */ }

```

And then again for `utf16_len`.
